hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19170","Ali ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Man ibn Muhammad ibn Man ibn Nadla ibn Amr al-Ghifari, a Medinan, narrated to me, he said: My grandfather Muhammad ibn Man narrated to me, from his father Man ibn Nadla, from Nadla ibn Amr al-Ghifari, that he met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Marrayn(?), and milch she-camels of his rushed upon him. So he gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink, then drank the remainder of a vessel and was filled with it. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I used to drink seven yet not be filled. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer drinks in one intestine, and the disbeliever drinks in seven intestines."
